From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:47:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add quad-buffer stereo rendering

Add the render.stereo option, with --stereo, to render the scene through
OpenGL quad-buffer stereo (GL_BACK_LEFT and GL_BACK_RIGHT), and the
render.stereo_eye_angle option, with --stereo-eye-angle, for the angle
between the eyes, which is the eye angle of the camera.

The window is realized when the engine is created, before the options are
known, so it is recreated once, before the first render, as a stereo
capable window. Nothing changes with the option off.

Assisted-by: glm-5.3:cloud (Ollama) via Codex
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
